{"name":"Bridgeport","hex":"#004683","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bridgeport","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A settlement in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada.","A neighbourhood on Cape Breton Island, Nova Scotia, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bridgeport"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bridgeport, Connecticut","blocks":[{"text":"Bridgeport is the most populous city in the U.S. state of Connecticut. The population was 148,654 in 2020, making it the fifth-most populous city in New England. It is a port city in eastern Fairfield County at the mouth of the Pequonnock River on Long Island Sound, 60 miles (97 km) from Manhattan and 40 miles (64 km) from The Bronx. Bridgeport and other towns in Fairfield County make up the Greater Bridgeport Planning Region, as well as the Bridgeport–Stamford–Norwalk–Danbury metropolitan statistical area, the second largest metropolitan area in Connecticut and a component of the greater New York metropolitan area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Bridgeport%2C_Connecticut_downtown.jpg/330px-Bridgeport%2C_Connecticut_downtown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridgeport%2C_Connecticut"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/BridgeportCT_SeasidePark_PerryMemorialArch.jpg/500px-BridgeportCT_SeasidePark_PerryMemorialArch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/BridgeportCT_SeasidePark_PerryMemorialArch.jpg/500px-BridgeportCT_SeasidePark_PerryMemorialArch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABridgeportCT_SeasidePark_PerryMemorialArch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Metro-North_New_Haven_Line_tr